.TH JWT-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "jwt-audit 0.3.0" "Security Tools"
.SH NAME
jwt-audit \- active and offline JSON Web Token security auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jwt-audit scan
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jwt-audit inspect
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jwt-audit
discovers protected HTTP endpoints and tests whether they accept unsigned JWTs
or tokens signed with weak, empty, or null-like HMAC candidate keys. Deep scans
also test malformed and ambiguous algorithm headers. It inspects compact
JWTs offline for unsafe algorithms, weak candidate secrets, sensitive claims,
and missing validation claims.
.SH SCAN PROFILES
.TP
.B safe
Tests only explicitly supplied endpoints with two short-lived HS256 payloads.
.TP
.B standard
Discovers common API and administration endpoints and tests the full identity
and privilege mutation matrix with HS256 and two header orderings.
.TP
.B deep
Adds more endpoints and payloads, HS384, HS512, and unsigned-token checks.
It also enables algorithm/parser mutations. Empty/null key checks are enabled
by default in both standard and deep profiles.
.SH SELECTED OPTIONS
.TP
.B --secret-file FILE
Add newline-delimited HMAC candidate secrets.
.TP
.B --openapi FILE
Import endpoint paths from an OpenAPI JSON or YAML document.
.TP
.B --endpoint-pack NAME
Add a curated endpoint family. This option is repeatable.
.TP
.B --fuzz-template PATH
Expand FUZZ in a path using the built-in or supplied wordlist.
.TP
.B --fuzz-wordlist FILE
Use newline-delimited replacements for FUZZ templates.
.TP
.B --payload-file FILE
Add a JSON, YAML, or JSON Lines claims corpus.
.TP
.B --method METHOD
Set endpoint discovery and test method order. This option is repeatable.
.TP
.B --rate N
Set a global maximum request rate per second.
.TP
.B --max-requests N
Stop after this many HTTP attempts, including retries.
.TP
.B --max-runtime SECONDS
Stop when the runtime budget is exhausted and report partial results.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print endpoint, payload, candidate, and limiter counts without network traffic.
.TP
.B --confusion-key FILE
Test an approved RSA public key or certificate as an HMAC secret.
.TP
.B --include-key-edge-cases
Test empty, null-byte, and literal-null HMAC keys. The corresponding
--no-include-key-edge-cases form disables them.
.TP
.B --include-algorithm-mutations
Test mixed-case none, empty signatures, missing/null algorithms, and duplicate
algorithm members. The corresponding --no-include-algorithm-mutations form
disables them.
.TP
.B --token-cookie NAME
Send JWT candidates in the named cookie instead of the Authorization header.
.TP
.B --header NAME:VALUE
Add a static request header. This option is repeatable.
.TP
.B --proxy URL
Send requests through an HTTP or HTTPS interception proxy.
.TP
.B --deny-pattern TEXT
Treat response bodies containing this text as access denials.
.TP
.B --format text|json|sarif
Select the report format.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
jwt-audit scan --target https://staging.example.test --profile standard \
  --acknowledge-authorization I_HAVE_AUTHORIZATION
.PP
jwt-audit scan --target https://lab.example.test --profile deep \
  --secret-file candidates.txt --format sarif --output report.sarif \
  --acknowledge-authorization I_HAVE_AUTHORIZATION
.PP
jwt-audit inspect --token-file token.txt --common-secrets
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means no finding, 1 means an operational error, and 2 means one or more
findings were produced.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
Active scanning must only be performed on systems the operator owns or has
explicit permission to test.
.SH AUTHOR
Liam Giannini, Webcracy.ch.
